    "notes": [
      "t01 is TB7's own example — feat then fix then test, one turn, one file — and the case the guards are there for. t04 is the case they fire on and this annotation disagrees with: a conventional-type change 20 minutes later on a path the first commit never touched, which TB7 reads as a new turn and the annotator reads as one turn finishing its own sentence. It is in the corpus to count that disagreement, not to hide it: it is one of the five false splits message-shape makes over the whole corpus.",
      "t06 and t07 have byte-identical subjects and the same author, so their identities are equal and their boundary is a TB10 twin pair: two episodes with ids `ep-x` and `ep-x-2`, which is the corpus's check that identity and boundary are different questions."
    ]
